  "goodToKnow": "Obdachlos means homeless, literally without shelter (das Obdach, a literary word). Der/die Obdachlose is a homeless person, and die Obdachlosigkeit homelessness. Around 50,000 people in Germany sleep rough or with no fixed housing, according to a 2024 government report; many more are wohnungslos, living in shelters. Street papers like Hinz&Kunzt in Hamburg are sold by homeless vendors. Cities run Kältehilfe in winter."
